## Primary owner
Codex/Astra as independent reviewer/test author. Do not implement Claude-owned feature code unless a follow-up issue explicitly assigns it.

## Depends on
Run incrementally after #2–#6 produce reviewable branches/PRs.

## Goal
Independently verify that Phase 1 implementation matches repository architecture and failure-safety requirements.

## Review checklist
- package dependency direction from ADR-008;
- no Prisma/Meta/React imports in `packages/domain`;
- no Meta-specific fields leaking into channel-neutral application logic;
- tenant/workspace isolation tests;
- webhook idempotency and duplicate enqueue behavior;
- BullMQ deterministic IDs and safe retry semantics;
- no blocking sleeps in webhooks;
- ambiguous-send path never blindly retries;
- secret/env validation and no committed credentials;
- TypeScript strictness and exhaustive union handling.

## Independent test additions
Prefer adding tests in separate review/test branches for uncovered invariants, especially concurrency, duplicate events, cross-workspace isolation, superseded jobs and malformed external payloads.

## Deliverable
For each reviewed PR, produce a concise review record: PASS / CHANGES_REQUESTED with exact file/line or test evidence. If a systemic architecture mismatch is found, propose an ADR/spec amendment rather than silently normalizing it in code.

From spec 0089 (#89, PR #91), accepted by the owner on 2026-10-09 as a follow-up.

## Why

Under ADR 0029 a free-agent start counts toward the start replacement level only when the pitcher was a starter on his earlier appearances of the season. The fixtures hold two consecutive days, so no start in them can qualify. In CI, after #89:

- the start pool is empty and its level is null;
- every fixture start has a null value, by the model's rule for an empty pool;
- `int_fantasy__replacement_pool_has_played_days` warns (CI warnings go from 3 to 4);
- `rec_fantasy__category_wins_added` cannot re-score a pair with a start.

Unit tests cover the rule and the real build exercises it. What CI no longer does is compute starters' values end to end.

## What is needed

A third fixture day, earlier in the season than the two there are, with MLB boxscores in which at least one pitcher who is a free agent in the fixture league starts on it and again on one of the existing days. It only needs MLB data for the earlier day (the rule reads a pitcher's MLB history, not rosters), unless the scoring-date logic requires a roster for it: to be checked.

Generated by `scripts/make_fixtures.py` from landed captures by the existing allowlists; the multi-league tree and the isolation check follow. See how #74 handled moving fixture days.

## Done when

- CI's start pool has played days and the warning above is gone;
- fixture starts have a value;
- no existing fixture file changes except by the generator.
